  Final report:
    uSync exported the full schema automatically (ContentTypes, DataTypes, Templates, Media, Content under `uSync/v18/`). Everything is done and verified. The site is still running.
    
    ## Report
    
    **What I built** — a working blog site in Umbraco.Bench, modeled and published entirely through the two MCP servers:
    
    - **Schema** (`umbraco`): three block element types (`richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock`) filed in the Blocks folder; a `Blog Block Grid` data type (12 columns, all three blocks, read back to confirm); `blogFrontPage` and `blogPost` page types in the Pages folder; templates wired via `update-document-type`; content tree `siteRoot → blogFrontPage → blogPost` with allowed children set accordingly.
    - **Media** (`umbraco`): a `Blog Images` folder with 4 Unsplash photos imported.
    - **Content** (`umbraco-editor`): a `Blog` front page under WWW and two published posts — *"Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Every Tool"* and *"Why MCP Is Awesome: Editors Get Superpowers Too"* — each with title, publish date, excerpt, listing image, and a 4-block body (rich text → image → rich text → quote). The front page has a title, intro, and a rich text block, and lists both posts (newest first) with link, title, date, excerpt, and cropped listing image.
    - **Domain**: `/` (en-US) assigned to the front page, so it answers at the site root.
    - **Rendering** (per AGENTS.md's pipeline): `Views/blogFrontPage.cshtml` and `Views/blogPost.cshtml` filled in place as full HTML pages rendering `@await Html.GetBlockGridHtmlAsync(Model, "body")`; three adapter-only partials in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/` mapping `BlockGridItem<T>` to plain models in `Models/Blocks/`; three ViewComponents (`ViewComponents/`) with markup in `Views/Shared/Components/<Name>/Default.cshtml`; Tailwind classes throughout, built via `npm run build` into `wwwroot/dist/site.css`.
    
    **How to view it** — Umbraco is running right now: open **https://localhost:44317/** (front page) and the two post URLs linked from it. To restart later: `cd Umbraco.Bench.Umbraco && dotnet run`. Backoffice: `/umbraco` (admin@example.com / 1234567890 — the scaffold default, change before anything real).
    
    **Verified with curl** — `/` and both posts return **200**; every block renders (8 paragraphs, figure+caption, blockquote per post; post cards on the front page); no literal `<p>` tags (rich text prints via `@Html.Raw`); no "Could not render component"; all images and the stylesheet return 200. `dotnet build` succeeds; uSync exported the schema.
    
    **Issues hit and fixed** (none outstanding):
    1. `RichTextBlockModel` was ambiguous with Umbraco core's own `Umbraco.Cms.Core.Models.Blocks.RichTextBlockModel` in the adapters — fixed with a `using` alias in each adapter partial.
    2. `publish-page` with `includeDescendants: true` returned "Publish cancelled" once; publishing the front page alone, then each post individually, worked (posts require their parent published first).
    
    **Not working / caveats**: nothing. One cosmetic note: the scaffold's `umb-block-grid` classes carry no CSS (per instructions I added none), so blocks stack full-width — each component view carries its own `my-8` spacing, which looks fine.

