    Everything verified. The site is running — final report:
    
    ## Report
    
    **What I built** — a blog site on the Umbraco.Bench project, modeled and filled entirely through the two MCP servers:
    
    **Schema (umbraco)**
    - 3 block element types, moved into the Blocks folder: `richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock`
    - `Blog Block Grid` data type (12 columns, all three blocks allowed at root and in areas) — read back and verified
    - 2 templates (`blogFrontPage`, `blogPost`) and 2 page types in the Pages folder
    - `siteRoot` now allows `blogFrontPage`; `blogFrontPage` allows `blogPost` with default templates set — all read back and verified
    - Media folder `Blog` with 5 Unsplash photos imported
    
    **Content (umbraco-editor)**
    - "MCP Blog" front page under WWW: title, intro, one rich text block, and a listing of its posts
    - Two posts, each with 4 blocks in order (rich text → image with caption/credit → rich text → quote): *Why MCP Is Awesome* and *MCP in Practice: Building This Blog*
    - All three pages published; domain `/` (en-US) set on the front page and verified
    
    **Code**
    - ModelsBuilder generated `BlogFrontPage`, `BlogPost`, `RichTextBlock`, `ImageBlock`, `QuoteBlock` (both builds: 0 errors)
    - Plain view models in `Models/Blocks/`, one ViewComponent per block in `ViewComponents/` with views in `Views/Shared/Components/<Name>/Default.cshtml`
    - Adapters in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/<alias>.cshtml` (alias-cased filenames) — mapping only, no markup
    - `Views/blogFrontPage.cshtml` / `blogPost.cshtml` filled in place: full HTML pages, `GetBlockGridHtmlAsync(Model, "body")`, front page lists posts with link/date/excerpt/cropped listing image; Tailwind classes throughout
    - Frontend built: `npm install` + `npm run build` → `dist/site.css` (12 kB) and `dist/main.js`
    
    **Verified by curl** — all three URLs return **200** (`/`, `/why-mcp-is-awesome/`, `/mcp-in-practice-building-this-blog/`):
    - Front page: both post links, both dates, versioned `site.css` link
    - Posts: 4 block items each, correct alias mix, both paragraphs' text present as rendered HTML (`<p>` in markup, not escaped), blockquote and image credit rendering
    - **Zero** "Could not render component" occurrences on any page
    - Cropped image URL and CSS both return 200
    
    **Notes**
    - One initial snag: creating the front page failed until `siteRoot`'s allowed children included `blogFrontPage` (I'd skipped that part of the cheat sheet) — fixed and verified.
    - The bulk publish-with-descendants was cancelled twice; publishing the three pages individually worked fine.
    - `dotnet build` shows pre-existing SixLabors.ImageSharp vulnerability warnings (not from my changes).
    - Umbraco is currently **running** in the background — view the site at **https://localhost:44317/** (accept the dev certificate).

