    **Schema (umbraco server)**
    - 3 blocks in the Blocks folder: `richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock`
    - `Blog Block Grid` data type (Umbraco.BlockGrid, 12 columns, all three blocks allowed at root and in areas)
    - 2 page types in the Pages folder: `blogFrontPage` (title, intro, body) and `blogPost` (title, publishDate, excerpt, listingImage, body), each with its template set as default
    - Templates `blogFrontPage` and `blogPost`
    - Note: the cheat sheet said "siteRoot allows blogFrontPage" — that required one extra `update-document-type` on the Site Root type, since it initially allowed no children (this is what blocked the first page creation with "Operation not permitted")
    
    **Media** — `Blog` folder with 5 Unsplash photos imported (code-on-screen, laptop-desk-code, connected-structure, network-lines-dots, circuit-board)
    
    **Content (umbraco-editor server)** — "Why MCP Is Awesome" front page under WWW (with domain `/`), and 2 posts under it, each with 4+ blocks: rich text → image → rich text → quote. All three pages published.
    
    **Code** — generated ModelsBuilder models, then the Razor pipeline per AGENTS.md: two page views, three `blockgrid/Components/` adapters, three ViewComponents with plain models in `Models/Blocks/`, Tailwind built via the frontend project.
    
    **Verified** (curl -k, all fresh):
    - `/`, `/mcp-turns-tools-into-teammates/`, `/one-protocol-every-assistant/` all return **200**
    - Every block renders on every page; zero "Could not render component"
    - No escaped/literal `<p>` tags anywhere
    - Signed `/media/...` image URLs return 200
    - Front page lists both posts with image, date, title, excerpt
    
    **Two issues hit and fixed**
    1. `publish-page` with `includeDescendants` was cancelled twice at its confirmation prompt; publishing each page individually went through.
    2. First render failed with the scaffold's "partial view could not be found" fallback — actually my ViewComponents were named `RichTextComponent` etc., which MVC doesn't discover (the class name must end in `ViewComponent`). Renamed and rebuilt; that fixed all blocks.
    
    **Not working:** nothing known. Umbraco is still running (`dotnet run`, background task) — the site is live at https://localhost:44317/ (dev admin: admin@example.com / 1234567890).

